cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "LowBit Trace Corpus (LTC): A Deterministic Branch-Prediction and Cache-Access Benchmark Suite for RISC-V"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mohanty
    given-names: "Om Pranab"
    affiliation: "Sri Sathya Sai Institute of Higher Learning (SSSIHL)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-16"
license: LicenseRef-LICENSE.md
repository: "local"
keywords:
  - RISC-V
  - branch-prediction
  - cache-performance
  - microarchitecture
  - benchmark-suite
  - machine-learning
  - performance-modeling
abstract: >
  A 500-program deterministic, portable benchmark suite crossing 50
  branch-prediction patterns with 50 cache-access patterns across
  four working-set size tiers, designed to produce labeled CPU traces
  for training and evaluating machine learning models that predict
  branch-misprediction and cache-hit/miss behavior. Generator-driven
  (five Python catalogue scripts plus a shared template), backend-
  agnostic (no benchmark source file contains hardware-counter or
  simulator-specific code), with an explicit warm-up / region-of-
  interest / validation lifecycle and a documented, versioned output
  schema.
